# What Vercel does NOT need. Two reasons this file exists, and the second one
# matters more than the size of the upload:
#
# 1. Vercel turns every file in a top-level api/ directory into a serverless
#    function. That directory is also the FastAPI app -- api/main.py and
#    friends -- and Vercel would try to build each of those as a Python
#    function, on an image with no trimesh, manifold3d or scikit-image. The
#    only thing in there meant to be deployed is insights.js.
# 2. The build only ever runs `npm --prefix web`, so none of the Python, the
#    profiles, the corpus or the design masters is reachable from it anyway.
api/*.py
api/__pycache__/
prep/
tests/
bench/
spikes/
design/
docs/
var/
output/
.venv/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
Dockerfile
requirements*.txt
pyproject.toml
result.json
my-printer.txt

# The check harness for api/insights.js. It lives in web/ precisely so Vercel
# does not see it as a function, but it is test-only either way.
web/insights-check.mjs
web/flatten-check.mjs
web/parts-check.mjs
web/framing-check.mjs
